#: model_terms:ir.actions.act_window,help:om_hr_payroll.action_contribution_register_form
msgid ""
"A contribution register is a third party involved in the salary\n"
"                payment of the employees. It can be the social security, the\n"
"                state or anyone that collect or inject money on payslips."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model:ir.model.constraint,message:om_hr_payroll.constraint_hr_rule_parameter_value_parameter_date_uniq
msgid "A rule parameter can only have one value per date."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model_terms:ir.actions.act_window,help:om_hr_payroll.action_hr_rule_parameter
msgid ""
"A rule parameter holds a rate, a threshold or a ceiling by date. Changing it next year is\n"
"                entering a value, not editing the code of a rule, and the payslips of this year keep the value\n"
"                of this year."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model:ir.model.constraint,message:om_hr_payroll.constraint_hr_salary_bracket_version_bracket_date_key_uniq
msgid "A salary bracket can only have one table per date and key."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model_terms:ir.actions.act_window,help:om_hr_payroll.action_hr_salary_bracket
msgid ""
"A salary bracket holds the bands of a tax or of a contribution by date, and a rule computes an\n"
"                amount from it in one line. The bands of the previous years stay, so an old payslip computed\n"
"                again is still right."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model:ir.model.constraint,message:om_hr_payroll.constraint_hr_version_salary_component_version_component_uniq
msgid "A salary component can only be set once on a version."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model_terms:ir.actions.act_window,help:om_hr_payroll.action_hr_salary_component
msgid ""
"A salary component, e.g. a housing or a transport component, holds an amount on the contract of\n"
"                the employee. The salary rules read it with components.&lt;CODE&gt;, so the same rules serve\n"
"                every company whatever it pays."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:om_hr_payroll.hr_salary_bracket_view_form
msgid ""
"A table applies from its date on. Use the key when the same scale has a table\n"
"                                per filing status, per state or per pay frequency, and leave it empty\n"
"                                otherwise. The last band has no upper limit: leave its To at zero."
msgstr ""

#. module: om_hr_payroll
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:om_hr_payroll.hr_rule_parameter_view_form
msgid ""
"A value applies from its date until the next one. A payslip computed again for\n"
"                                an old period keeps the value of that period."
msgstr ""

